  <main class="detail-main" id="main" tabindex="-1"><div class="detail-hero"><div class="wrap detail-hero-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/journal/">Journal</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Three questions to ask about dental ozone</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">Biological care · 3 min read</p><h1>Three questions to ask about dental ozone</h1><p class="detail-lead">If dental ozone comes up in a treatment discussion, ask what role the dentist proposes for it and what the rest of the plan includes.</p></div></div><div class="wrap detail-grid"><article class="detail-card prose"><p class="editorial-note" data-editorial-review>Staging only — this article is hidden from the public site until clinically approved in the Raina Website settings.</p><section><h2>What is it being used for in my visit?</h2><p>Ask for a description of the dental finding and the specific purpose of adding ozone. If several procedures are planned, ask the dentist to walk through the sequence and explain where the ozone step would fit.</p></section><section><h2>What can we reasonably expect?</h2><p>Ask what evidence applies to that particular use, what the limits are and which risks or uncertainties matter in your case. It is reasonable to ask how the dentist would evaluate whether the overall treatment is working.</p></section><section><h2>What are the alternatives?</h2><p>Ask what the standard options are, how they compare and what follow-up would look like with each. Those answers can help you decide what questions to take away and consider before proceeding.</p></section><a class="text-link" href="/care/ozone/">Explore dental ozone at Raina <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></article><aside class="detail-aside"><span class="aside-mark" aria-hidden="true">R</span><p class="eyebrow">Raina Dental Care</p><h2>Let’s talk.</h2><p>2323 Naperville Road, Sui